# NET-MESH-0 pass 1: the DesertServer target on macOS (Docs/contracts/NET-ARCH.md §6, §9 row NET-MESH-0).
# Outside the editor (DesertEngine-scratch/NET-MESH-0/; the world is a COPY of WP_Protocol under world/ with its
# __ExternalEntities__/WP_Protocol, _Landscape and _HLOD, cp -p, so the cook never writes into the repo):
#   build/Bin/Debug/WorldCook world/WP_Protocol.desce
#        --out world/WP_Protocol.dwworld --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --project-registry
#   build/Bin/Debug/DesertServer --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --role all
#        --world <scratch>/world/WP_Protocol.desce --source 0,0,0 --steps 600   > mesh0_mac_server.log
#   otool -L build/Bin/Debug/DesertServer                                     > mesh0_mac_server.otool.txt
# Тогда [mesh0_mac_server]: the log shows "no device created", the cooked index loaded with its cook hash, 600 steps
# at 60 Hz and the residency union of one source; the otool list names no Vulkan/MoltenVK/Metal/AppKit/Cocoa.
# Pass 3 (Тогда [mesh0_core_split]): DesertServer links the module Core (render-free, configure-checked) instead
# of a source list; the same run gives the same cook hash and 600 steps, otool -L > mesh0_core_split.otool.txt.
# Regression (here): the client still builds and opens WP_Protocol unchanged (ReadCookedWorld moved to CookedWorld).
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
Дано state
# Тогда [mesh0_core_split] (вне редактора): mesh0_core_split.otool.txt без Vulkan/MoltenVK/Metal/AppKit; mesh0_core_split.log: no device created, cook hash ee311acb3b50b349, 600 steps
Тогда mesh0_editor_wp_protocol WP_Protocol как в dev: ландшафт, город, кусты, небо; без падения и диалога ошибки
